  "label": "The text 'the reich' is mapped onto the visual entity Adolf Hitler",
  "description": "The overlaid text 'can you smell what the reich is cooking?' uses the term 'the reich' to refer to the Nazi regime, which is visually represented by Adolf Hitler. The meme maps the abstract concept of 'the reich' (a political entity responsible for genocide) onto the specific visual entity of Adolf Hitler, who is depicted in a mundane, casual activity (picnicking). This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent, as it equates the monstrous historical figure with the abstract concept of the regime he led, thereby trivializing the Holocaust and invoking antisemitic stereotypes.",
